  [RISK] arch/riscv/kernel/crash_save_regs.S:46-54  riscv_crash_save_regs
      Saves CSR_TVAL into PT_BADADDR during kexec crash register capture. If the crash was triggered from a PMP violation access fault with paging enabled, badaddr in the crash dump contains the VA, not PA. Crash analysis tools (e.g., crash(8), drgn) that display PT_BADADDR as a physical address in the access-fault context would misdiagnose the fault. The save does not record satp.MODE or any indicator of whether the value is VA or PA.
