  [OK] arch/riscv/kvm/vcpu_exit.c:15-25  gstage_page_fault
      Reconstructs fault_addr from trap->htval (GPA, shifted left by 2 to recover full GPA from the WARL-truncated htval) and trap->stval (GVA, only low 2 bits used for offset within page). This is a textbook-correct example of treating the two trap-value registers with distinct type semantics: htval carries a guest-physical address, stval carries a guest-virtual address. The code correctly distinguishes them and composes the full fault address. Confirms that when code respects the type semantics of each trap-value register, no confusion occurs.
  [RISK] arch/riscv/kvm/vcpu_switch.S:250-271  __kvm_riscv_unpriv_trap
